<!--
  RM_LongShade_Fauna.xml                    LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1, Q1

  The 13 invented-name Long Shade animals the 2026-09-27 sitting ruled onto
  this tier (bokka, ossik, kudda, thurra, vosska, khorrak, ommok, ulgga,
  jellypot, truffle mole [pikkut], great devourer, groundrunner, mature
  fleshbeast — the 14th, the shade whale/Gloomcast, has its own file,
  RM_LongShade_Gloomcast.xml, because its body/leather/texture are shared
  with RSW_Horax and needed duplicating rather than a straight rename).

  Moved out of src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/DesertPort/RSW_DesertPortMisc_Races.xml
  and src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/BiomesTeamPort/ThingDefs_Races/RSW_BiomesTeamPort_Races.xml
  (bokka, jellypot, truffle mole) and standalone RSW_GreatDevourer.xml /
  RSW_Groundrunner.xml / RSW_MatureFleshbeast.xml, defNames renamed RSW_ -> RM_.
  Labels UNCHANGED — the batch-4c naming sitting rules on labels, not this item.

  Satellite defs each creature needs exclusively (eggs, the kudda's cactus
  leather/meat, the great devourer's armoured-worm body) moved and renamed
  alongside their creature; they live in RM_LongShade_FaunaSupport.xml so this
  file stays races-only, matching every other RimMandrake biome mod's shape.

  Per-creature simplifications made moving tiers (each also noted at its own
  ThingDef, and in the LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 closing report):
    - kudda: leatherDef/specificMeatDef repointed off the shared RSW_CactusHide/
      RSW_CactusMeat (still used by two SW-tier creatures that are not moving)
      onto this mod's own RM_CactusHide/RM_CactusMeat duplicates.
    - vosska: leatherDef Leather_RaptorPlates was a pre-existing dangling
      reference (no ThingDef anywhere in this repo defines it) — corrected to
      Leather_Bear in passing.
    - khorrak: the RSW-tier steel-diet comp (RimMandrake.StarWars.SWBestiary.
      CompProperties_MetalEater) and its useMeatFrom (RSW_Korrum, staying SW-
      tier) are dropped — cross-mod references the free mod cannot carry. Diet
      falls back to plain VegetarianRoughAnimal grazing.
    - jellypot / truffle mole: their shared RSW-tier LifeStageDefs
      (RSW_EusocialInsectAdult, RSW_DiggerBaby/Juvenile/Adult — both used by
      other SW-tier creatures that are not moving) are repointed onto the
      vanilla stages every other creature in this file already uses
      (EusocialInsectAdult, AnimalBaby/Juvenile/Adult); their per-species
      RSW_Biomes_*_Wounded/Death/Call/Angry SoundDefs are dropped (cosmetic,
      cross-mod) rather than duplicated.
    - mature fleshbeast: useMeatFrom AA_Helixien and the AA_TarGuzzler_* sound
      refs were ALREADY dangling (Alpha Animals donor defNames this repo never
      ported) — dropped rather than carried forward broken into a new tier.

  🔴 LONGSHADE_SHEET_STRUCTURAL_RULINGS_1 (2026-10-05): kudda, ossik, thurra and
  mature fleshbeast were CUT (defs deleted); jellypot/groundrunner renamed
  RM_Dunejelly/RM_Oreclaw; ommok (Miasma), truffle mole (Leaning Scrub), ulgga
  and vosska (Stillsand) are cast elsewhere but their defs stay in this file.

  Art: every texPath below is unchanged from the RSW_ file it moved from — no
  art job filed by this item for these 13; several still point at "TEMP
  PLACEHOLDER" donor textures or an unrendered RM_<Name>/RM_<Name> path,
  exactly as they did before the move. Check
  infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending}/registry.jsonl before filing a fresh
  job (CLAUDE.md's "check for existing regenerated art" rule) — this pass did
  not search per-creature beyond bokka/ossik/etc's existing placeholder state.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Bokka</defName>
    <label>bokka</label>
    <description>These large reptile-like animals normally feed on the likes of cacti. If angered, however, their durable hide makes them quite difficult to kill.\n\nTheir longer back legs and strange appearance lends credence to the belief that they were engineered to live in arid environments. Why they live underground, however, is uncertain.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>3.25</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>250</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>0</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>60</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ToxicEnvironmentResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.95</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
      <Wildness>0.5</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>left claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>8</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftClaws</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>8</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightClaws</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>10</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.7</chanceFactor>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>5</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
