	<ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
		<!-- LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1, Q1 tier move: RSW_Khorrak -> RM_Khorrak (was Alpha Animals AA_Terramorph, ported RSW_-tier 2026-09-20). The RSW-tier steel-diet comp (RimMandrake.StarWars.SWBestiary.CompProperties_MetalEater) and its useMeatFrom (RSW_Korrum, an SW-tier creature staying in the Utinni layer) are DROPPED moving to this tier — both are cross-mod references the free RM_LongShade mod cannot carry. Stats/body/tools are unchanged; the khorrak eats VegetarianRoughAnimal like any other RM-tier grazer instead of steel. Mechanic simplification, same shape as every other donor-framework drop this cast already took on the way in. -->
		<defName>RM_Khorrak</defName>
		<label>khorrak</label>
		<description>A strange crustacean bred for one purpose: mineral processing. The khorrak feeds on iron compounds, chemically working them into vacstone, a dense stone otherwise found only in asteroids. The transmutation is slow: every few days a khorrak sheds a chunk of vacstone where it rests.</description>
		<statBases>
			<MoveSpeed>1.8</MoveSpeed>
			<ComfyTemperatureMin>-40</ComfyTemperatureMin>
			<MarketValue>250</MarketValue>
			<ArmorRating_Blunt>0.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
			<ArmorRating_Sharp>0.75</ArmorRating_Sharp>
			<LeatherAmount>0</LeatherAmount>
			<MeatAmount>0</MeatAmount>
			<Wildness>0.65</Wildness>
		</statBases>
		<tools>
			<li>
				<label>fangs</label>
				<capacities>
					<li>Bite</li>
				</capacities>
				<power>14</power>
				<cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
				<linkedBodyPartsGroup>TurtleBeakAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
			</li>
			<li>
				<label>head</label>
				<capacities>
					<li>Blunt</li>
				</capacities>
				<power>4</power>
				<cooldownTime>1.65</cooldownTime>
				<linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
				<chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
			</li>
		</tools>
		<race>
			<body>TurtleLike</body>
			<herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
			<predator>false</predator>
			<baseBodySize>1.5</baseBodySize>
			<baseHealthScale>1</baseHealthScale>
			<baseHungerRate>0.1</baseHungerRate>
			<foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
			<trainability>None</trainability>
			<lifeExpectancy>15</lifeExpectancy>
			<lifeStageAges>
				<li><def>AnimalBaby</def><minAge>0</minAge></li>
				<li><def>AnimalJuvenile</def><minAge>0.1</minAge></li>
				<li><def>AnimalAdult</def><minAge>0.2222</minAge></li>
			</lifeStageAges>
			<soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
			<soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
			<soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
		</race>
		<comps>
			<li Class="CompProperties_Spawner">
				<!-- LONGSHADE_SHEET_STRUCTURAL_RULINGS_1, owner 2026-10-04: "It should produce vacstone chunks." Vanilla CompSpawner (precedent on a pawn: AA_Eyeling, Ikee_Tuning.xml). ChunkVacstone is Odyssey (all DLC assumed). One chunk per 4-6 days; spawnMaxAdjacent keeps a resting khorrak from piling them. -->
				<thingToSpawn>ChunkVacstone</thingToSpawn>
				<spawnCount>1</spawnCount>
				<spawnIntervalRange>240000~360000</spawnIntervalRange>
				<spawnMaxAdjacent>2</spawnMaxAdjacent>
				<writeTimeLeftToSpawn>true</writeTimeLeftToSpawn>
				<showMessageIfOwned>false</showMessageIfOwned>
				<saveKeysPrefix>khorrakVacstone</saveKeysPrefix>
			</li>
		</comps>
		<tradeTags>
			<li>AnimalUncommon</li>
		</tradeTags>
	</ThingDef>

